President Donald Trump vowed a political comeback on Sunday after Republicans lost control of Congress in last Tuesday’s midterms, as incoming Democratic leaders pledged to hold his administration to account, and the attorney general promised to defend officials against threatened prosecutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83a1ad10-dc2a-11f1-8764-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311694095065.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83a1ad10-dc2a-11f1-8764-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311694095065.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89efa1a6-dbd8-11f1-a76e-03031a2f4c21</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 01:13:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83a1ad10-dc2a-11f1-8764-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311694095065.jpg">© Phelan M. Ebenhack, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Nvidia shares tumble as CEO faces probe over affair with alleged Chinese spy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-nvidia-shares-slide-as-board-probes-ceo-over-china-spy-reports</link><description>
Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang is facing scrutiny after reports he was targeted in a suspected Chinese intelligence operation involving a businesswoman with whom he was having an affair. The controversy has rattled investors, sending Nvidia shares tumbling.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c09d2a-cd50-11f1-a2da-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/6816aa54a64f20da410fe06c62ff522af2f50eb2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c09d2a-cd50-11f1-a2da-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/6816aa54a64f20da410fe06c62ff522af2f50eb2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7015c2d6-dbc6-11f1-99b3-1507708d4bc0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 22:47:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c09d2a-cd50-11f1-a2da-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/6816aa54a64f20da410fe06c62ff522af2f50eb2.jpg">© John MacDougall, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo criticises Milei’s austerity in Argentina, says growth must benefit all</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-argentina-visit-milei</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV arrived in Argentina on Sunday from Uruguay, where his Latin America tour began, facing calls to help bridge divisions after three years of austerity under President Javier Milei. The visit to Buenos Aires is the first by a pontiff to the late Pope Francis’s homeland in nearly four decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c453da6-dc10-11f1-9232-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6V94TC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c453da6-dc10-11f1-9232-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6V94TC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4209491c-dbc1-11f1-8d7e-cd9c7bda3277</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 22:23:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c453da6-dc10-11f1-9232-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6V94TC.jpg">© Tiziani Fabi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal politics and Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261108-pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru</link><description>
After wrapping up his first visit to Uruguay, Pope Leo XIV heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his papacy so far. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and co-host of the "Inside the Vatican" podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of Leo's Latin American tour.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b628278a-dbb9-11f1-ac32-4364c774d43a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:16:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alessandro XENOS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo urges men to respect wives amid Latin American femicide crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV urged men to respect their wives as he wrapped up the first leg of his 12-day tour of Latin America. The region recorded nearly 20,000 instances of women being killed over the past five years alone, most of them murdered by a current or former partner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e95bad06-db7e-11f1-94ec-63ab1173e7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:15:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg">© Rodrigo Arangua, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paraguay: Senate impeached Peña rather than accept his offer to resign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe%C3%B1a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign</link><description>
Paraguay's ousted president, Santiago Peña, has been charged over the collapse of Ueno Bank. Initially placed under house arrest, he has since been transferred to a military facility for his own safety. Nearly three million customers were locked out of their accounts after regulators seized control of the online bank. Repayments are now under way, but protests continue as customers demand access to their money. Peña denies any wrongdoing. Jack Pownall reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97992746-db60-11f1-b875-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111033-111218-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97992746-db60-11f1-b875-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111033-111218-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c89fc9e-db60-11f1-b55f-b7e2ef7616a9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:42:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump wants UFC fighters as assistants</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-wants-ufc-fighters-as-assistants</link><description>
After a series of combative press briefings between the Trump administration and journalists, the US president surprised many by reportedly offering Dana White, the head of the Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) and a longtime friend, the role of White House press secretary. Trump praised White as a “violent fighter and warrior”, but US media reports say he has already turned down the offer. Was it a punchy choice by the president or simply a punchline? Jack Pownall takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad7ce2ee-db58-11f1-b2b1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-101159-101400-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad7ce2ee-db58-11f1-b2b1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-101159-101400-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b289ad26-db58-11f1-ae95-2ff3ce4ecc5e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:44:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'A violent fighter and warrior': Trump offers press secretary role to UFC chief Dana White</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-a-violent-fighter-and-warrior-trump-offers-press-secretary-role-to-ufc-chief-dana-white</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Saturday said he was asking mixed martial arts promoter Dana White to be the new White House press secretary. Trump has repeatedly tried to hitch his MAGA brand of politics to White's enormously successful Ultimate Fighting Championship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1699b72c-dadf-11f1-8689-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4336TP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1699b72c-dadf-11f1-8689-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4336TP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d329b48-dade-11f1-b828-3bf6f8d3d03e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 20:45:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1699b72c-dadf-11f1-8689-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4336TP.jpg">© Jim Watson, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
